    "body": "Great on any Friday: Baseus USB-A to USB-C Cable - Braided & Coiled (1.3 to 3.3 ft), Black/Red\nKoenigsegg Jesko Terrang Is a Virtual Take on the Sterrato & 911 Dakar From a Hypercar Perspective\n24 photos\nPhoto: abimelecdesign / Instagram\nAbimelec Arellano, a virtual artist better known as \" abimelecdesign \" on social media, has prepared the newest wishful-thinking project - a crazy supercar. The member of the imaginative guild of digital car content creators stopped dwelling across the parallel universes of vehicular design at the behest of a news outlet.\nThe good folks over at Motor1 came up with a wacky idea – “What if Koenigsegg built an off-road supercar to rival the Lamborghini Huracan Sterrato and Porsche 911 Dakar?” The Swedish automaker, an exotic company focused mainly on hypercars, is currently focused on a different thing - Christian von Koenigsegg took note of the recent BYD electric supercar top speed record and said that his brand still wants to push for a record-breaking run with the Jesko Absolut.\nThe latter theoretically can reach up to 330 mph, which is 532 kph, but it’s much harder to put it into practice: there are no tires capable of withstanding such extreme speeds. Just recently, BYD’s luxury brand Yangwang announced that its U9 Xtreme reached 312.65 mph (503.17 kph) on November 1.\nThe first production car that soared above the 310-mph (500-kph) threshold was officially recognized by the FIA, and the Chinese electric hypercar also has two Guinness World Records now, so it’s understandable why von Koenigsegg suddenly remembered their Jesko Absolut might be capable of more. Additionally, they now also have the financial means to pursue the record.\nAlso, recently Koenigsegg gained a new investment from a private equity firm, with the company now valued at around €1.3 billion ($1.4 billion at the current exchange rate). That also means they might be open to developing new versions – which is probably why the news outlet allied with the pixel master to imagine a potential new Jesko variant.\nDubbed the Terrang, it goes in a different direction – a mild off-road version that gives up some of the supercar prowess for a bit of “extra ground clearance and all-terrain capability.” They imagined the new version with a raised ride height, meaty off-road tires, and extra cladding for the lower parts of the body. However, the power setup would remain the same – 5.0-liter twin-turbo V8 with 1,280 hp or 1,600 hp on E85, just tuned for better low-rpm torque response.\nGiven the tremendous popularity of the Lamborghini Huracan Sterrato and Porsche 911 Dakar special editions, we shouldn’t exclude the possibility of more automakers going down that route – though nobody can tell for sure if Koenigsegg would be up for the task in the real world. So, what do you think – yay or nay? Or maybe they should just throw us a full-size SUV directly, just like McLaren is preparing to do? View this post on Instagram A post shared by Motor1.com (@motor1com)\nVia // Motor1\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nKoenigsegg Jesko Terrang Koenigsegg Jesko Koenigsegg jesko Terrang CGI supercar rendering abimelecdesign\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT 15 New Tarmac Works Collectibles You Can Buy Today",
